    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1544">

                <pb facs="1249" n="1133" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.00/349.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 6, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that little
                    of importance in the political situation has occurred since my arrival here and
                    that everything continues to center around the coming presidential elections,
                    notwithstanding their comparative remoteness. President Arosemena is apparently
                    most anxious to secure his reelection, and for the purpose of satisfying (as his
                    partisans claim) the constitutional requirement is generally expected to avail
                    himself early next month of the leave of absence granted to him by the Supreme
                    Court.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Percival Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
